旅游业怎么样？

294
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:58,000
We are seeing every year even more the travel rush
我们每年都能看到，尤其是在五一假期等长假期间，

295
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:02,000
during big holidays, such as the May Day holiday.
旅游高峰甚至更加明显。

296
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,000
What trends are forming there?
那里正在形成什么趋势？

297
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:11,000
Traveling is certainly a very big demand of the service sector.
旅游无疑是服务业中一个非常大的需求。

298
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:16,000
In old times people looked at the price and location,
过去人们看重价格和地点，

299
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:24,000
but in the future I think people will look at better services in travel.
但未来我认为人们会更看重旅游中的优质服务。

300
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:29,000
For example, they will probably use some AI tools
例如，他们可能会使用一些人工智能工具

301
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:35,000
to identify the best itinerary and to get the best place for shopping,
以规划最佳行程并找到最佳购物地点，

302
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:40,000
and to identify the place that there are no crowds, etc.
以及寻找没有人群拥挤的地方等。

303
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,000
So to improve the quality of the travel.
从而提升旅行质量。

304
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Also they will probably identify the local best restaurants, etc.
他们还会找出当地最好的餐厅等。

305
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:54,000
I think the quality and experience will be much improved in the future.
我认为未来的质量和体验会有很大提升。

306
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:59,000
As people become more sophisticated in terms of consuming services,
随着人们在消费服务方面变得更加成熟，

307
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:06,000
which brings us to the nation's drive to meet this kind of demand,
这也引出了国家为满足此类需求而采取的行动，

308
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:08,000
this kind of growing needs.
即满足这种不断增长的需求。

309
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:16,000
I was talking about the size of China's service sector, being about 12 trillion US dollars for last year.
我刚才提到中国服务业的规模，去年约为12万亿美元。

310
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:21,000
China has this planning system, so we have laid out the next five-year plan,
中国有规划体系，因此我们制定了下一个五年规划，

311
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:25,000
which is from 2025 to 2030.
即2025年至2030年。

312
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:34,000
It's expected that the service sector will grow to be as strong as 15 trillion US dollars.
预计服务业将增长至15万亿美元的强劲规模。

313
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
That's 100 trillion yuan.
即100万亿元人民币。

314
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:41,000
How does China have the confidence that it can achieve this goal?
中国凭什么有信心实现这一目标？

315
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:46,000
What will be the key drivers behind this growth?
推动这一增长的关键因素是什么？

316
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:53,000
First of all, from 12 trillion to 15 trillion in five years is not a big deal for China.
首先，从12万亿到15万亿，五年时间对中国来说不算什么大事。

317
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:59,000
It only takes 4-5% growth per year, so we will achieve that goal.
每年只需4%到5%的增长，我们就能实现这一目标。

318
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Second, I think with the technology development, in particular with the data technology and AI technology,
其次，我认为随着技术的发展，特别是数据技术和人工智能技术，

319
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:12,000
I think we will create a lot of new models for service in China.
我认为我们将在中国创造许多新的服务模式。

320
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Also, green service is also a big part of this service sector growth as well.
此外，绿色服务也是服务业增长的重要组成部分。

321
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:24,000
In China, also, we need a lot of high-value added service,
在中国，我们同样需要大量高附加值的服务，

322
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:32,000
high-quality service in healthcare, in senior care, in traveling, that you just mentioned.
包括医疗保健、老年护理以及您刚才提到的旅游等方面的高质量服务。

323
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:36,000
We do need a lot of high-value added service as well.
我们确实也需要大量高附加值的服务。

324
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:40,000
There's a lot of space to grow, new products, new services,
在增长方面还有很大空间，无论是新产品、新服务，

325
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:45,000
the combination of service and products, the combination of manufacturing services,
还是服务与产品的结合、制造与服务的结合，

326
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:52,000
as well as AI applications, generating new business models in the service sector.
以及人工智能应用，这些都在服务业催生出新的商业模式。

327
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:54,000
There's too much space to grow.
增长的空间太大了。

328
00:23:54,000 --> 00:24:00,000
I think this is a very conservative estimate to grow to 15 billion dollars.
我认为增长到150亿美元是一个非常保守的估计。

329
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:02,000
I think it could be 20 billion.
我觉得可能会达到200亿美元。

330
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,500
Wow.
哇。

331
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,000
If we do the right thing.
如果我们做对了的话。

332
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:11,000
As you mentioned, new things will emerge, for instance,
正如您提到的，将会涌现出新事物，例如，

333
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:15,000
new models and new consumption patterns.
新的模式和新的消费形态。

334
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:23,000
What could be some of the new consumption models and service scenarios that we can expect to emerge?
我们可以预期会出现哪些新的消费模式和服务场景？

335
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:28,000
How is that going to change people's way of leading their lives?
这将如何改变人们的生活方式？

336
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:33,000
There are just many things that could occur in the near future.
在不久的将来，可能会发生很多事情。

337
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:38,000
For example, the AI application in people's daily life,
例如，人工智能在日常生活中的应用，

338
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:43,000
we could use the AI agent to do the planning for our traveling,
我们可以使用AI智能体来规划我们的旅行，

339
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:50,000
and we use the AI for work to design the working schedule.
并利用AI来设计工作日程。

340
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Also, there will be integration of manufacturing and services.
此外，还将出现制造与服务的融合。

341
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:02,000
First of all, a lot of products will be sold along with a lot of service products.
首先，许多产品将伴随大量服务类产品一同销售。

342
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:08,000
For example, if you buy a car, then it could be like an AMAP tool on it,
例如，如果你买了一辆车，它可能就像上面装了一个高德地图工具，

343
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:12,000
and also connecting to a lot of other services.
并且还能连接许多其他服务。

344
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
If you buy a cell phone, it will come with other products, many manufacturing products as well.
如果你买了一部手机，它会附带其他产品，包括许多制造类产品。

345
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Secondly, I think in the manufacturing sector, we also need production service,
其次，我认为在制造业领域，我们也需要生产性服务，

346
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:32,000
which means we use the tools to provide to improve the efficiency in manufacturing,
这意味着我们利用工具来提升制造效率，

347
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:39,000
like planning, like scheduling, like logistics, like legal services,
比如规划、排程、物流、法律服务，

348
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:48,000
like strategy consulting, after-sales services, like compliance services, like risk management.
比如战略咨询、售后服务、合规服务、风险管理。

349
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:56,000
All these types of services for manufacturing for the goods production is also a big part of this.
所有这类服务于制造业和商品生产的服务，也是其中重要的一部分。

350
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:02,000
What kind of new scenarios are being created with the introduction of AI?
随着人工智能的引入，正在创造哪些新场景？

351
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:10,000
For instance, I was listening to Mr. Lee Gung from AMAP to talk about the introduction of AI technology into AMAPs,
例如，我听了高德地图的李刚先生谈论将人工智能技术引入高德地图，

352
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:12,000
so that people have greater experience.
以便让人们拥有更好的体验。

353
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:16,000
For instance, the Flying Street View feature of the map.
例如，地图中的飞行街景功能。

354
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:23,000
How are new scenarios being created, and what impact could this have?
新场景是如何被创造的，这可能带来什么影响？

355
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:27,000
I think the technology just makes our life much more colorful.
我认为技术只是让我们的生活变得更加丰富多彩。

356
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:32,000
Originally, for example, in AMAP, it would just give you the route to a destiny,
例如，最初在高德地图中，它只会给你到目的地的路线，

357
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:35,000
to a destiny, it would give you the best route for now.
到目的地，它会给你当前的最佳路线。

358
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:37,000
But now, it used to be just reactive.
但现在，它过去只是被动的。

359
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:41,000
You would give the app an order, they would give an answer.
你会给应用下达指令，它们会给出答案。

360
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:45,000
But in the future, it will be much more proactive and immersive.
但在未来，它将变得更加主动和沉浸式。

361
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:50,000
He could automatically provide other products and services for the suggestion,
它可以自动为建议提供其他产品和服务，

362
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:57,000
and also, it could make your experience much, much more immersive, like you're really in it.
而且，它能让你的体验变得更加沉浸，仿佛你真的身临其境。

363
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:01,000
This is a big change of our life.
这是我们要经历的一大生活变革。

364
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:08,000
What kind of opportunities is this AI plus services creating for foreign businesses?
这种“AI+服务”模式为外国企业创造了哪些机遇？

365
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:12,000
I understand the investment in high-tech sector,
我了解到，在高科技领域的投资，

366
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:19,000
especially for foreign direct investment, really shot up 30% in the first quarter of this year.
特别是外商直接投资，今年第一季度增长了30%。

367
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:24,000
What opportunities lie in AI plus services for foreign businesses?
对于外国企业来说，“AI+服务”蕴含着哪些机遇？

368
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:28,000
I think there's just a lot of opportunities for foreign investors as well.
我认为，外国投资者也拥有大量机遇。

369
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:32,000
For example, as I mentioned, there's a high-value added service.
例如，正如我提到的，存在高附加值的服务。

370
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:37,000
In China, the old model is very low-priced, long hours.
在中国，旧模式是低价格、长时间工作。

371
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,500
Cheap labor?
廉价劳动力？

372
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:39,500
Cheap labor.
廉价劳动力。

373
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:46,000
But now, with the assistance of AI, high-quality services will become much more accessible in China.
但现在，借助AI，在中国获得高质量服务将变得更加容易。

374
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:50,000
So, it certainly improved the quality of this kind of trade services.
因此，它确实提升了这类贸易服务的质量。

375
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:54,000
What kind of risks do you think there may be?
你认为可能存在哪些风险？

376
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,000
And what kind of bottlenecks?
以及哪些瓶颈？

377
00:27:56,000 --> 00:28:03,000
The biggest risk is probably the governance of new technology.
最大的风险可能是新技术的治理问题。

378
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Technology is neutral.
技术是中性的。

379
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:12,000
It could bring good things and also equally likely bring bad things.
它既能带来好事，也同样可能带来坏事。

380
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:17,000
So, for example, people use AI to improve their quality.
例如，人们利用AI来提升他们的质量。

381
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Certainly, we now see a lot of people use AI tool to cheat as well.
当然，我们现在也看到很多人使用人工智能工具来作弊。

382
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:28,000
And sometimes, our privacy is not well protected.
而且有时候，我们的隐私没有得到很好的保护。

383
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:32,000
So, this could be a big concern as well.
所以，这也是一个很大的担忧。

384
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:35,000
What's China's approach to addressing these bottlenecks?
中国如何应对这些瓶颈？

385
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:45,000
I think China should improve the legislation in this area for the governance in AI.
我认为中国应该完善这一领域的立法，以加强人工智能治理。

386
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:49,000
Also, try to break this local protectionism.
同时，努力打破地方保护主义。

387
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:56,000
Also, I think training workforce is important because not only we need people who have the new demand,
此外，我认为培养劳动力也很重要，因为我们不仅需要懂新需求的人，

388
00:28:56,000 --> 00:29:00,000
know the new demand, but also we need people who can provide these services.
还需要能提供这些服务的人。

389
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
We need to train people to learn the technology, how to use the new technology as well.
我们需要培训人们学习技术，以及如何运用新技术。

390
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:14,000
Okay. It's certainly a very big topic. We can't cover all, but I think we are trying to scratch the surface at least.
好的。这确实是一个非常大的话题。我们无法面面俱到，但我想我们至少已经触及了表面。

391
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Thank you so much, Professor He Ping, Associate Dean of the School of Economics and Management at Tsinghua University.
非常感谢何平教授，清华大学经济管理学院副院长。

392
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,500
Thank you.
谢谢。

393
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,000
Thank you.
谢谢。
